      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "🇺🇸 US claims non-interference in Bolsonaro's escape\n\nThe US did not assist Bolsonaro in leaving Brazil, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said, adding that Bolsonaro holds an American visa, so Donald Trump simply made the decision to let him into the country.\n\nHowever, media reports contradict the official statements from the White House:\n\n🔴 Bolsonaro's rush to the US was reportedly assisted by Donald Trump's political strategist Jason Miller, who organized the transfer from Argentina in a private jet, CNN Brazil writes\n\n🔴 The US allowed Bolsonaro to enter the country on an invalid diplomatic passport, as it had been canceled by the Brazilian government\n\n🔴 During the first part of the escape, he was also helped by a former Israeli Mossad agent who was in one of the vans with Bolsonaro and his family that crossed the Brazilian border\n\n💬 \"No plans to meet, but I think he got treated very shabbily. Very shabbily. So he can stay here as long as he wants,\" US President Donald Trump said when asked about possible talks with Bolsonaro.\n\nEarlier, Bolsonaro declared himself the leader of Brazil and described his departure as a \"strategy of struggle\" against a \"dictatorial regime.\" The politician also thanked US President Donald Trump and Argentine President Javier Milei for their support and hospitality.\n\n👍 Substack | Chat | @geopolitics_prime",
